{{!-- spec 025 (handoff "Anexar personagem") — the dropped character is named at
      the top, and the two roles ARE the buttons: one click answers, there is no
      confirm step. Each choice states what the role means, because "Leader" and
      "Attached Hero" alone do not say which one commands.

      The buttons live in the CONTENT (not in the frame's footer) so they can
      carry an icon, a label and a caption; the sheet binds them in the dialog's
      `render` hook — the same pattern the quality picker uses. --}}
<div class="cs-attach-dialog-body">
    <div class="cs-attach-subject">
        <img class="cs-attach-avatar" src="{{img}}" alt="{{name}}" />
        <div>
            <div class="cs-attach-name">{{name}}</div>
            <div class="cs-attach-question">{{localize "CS.dialogs.attachCharacter.hint"}}</div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="cs-attach-choices">
        <button type="button" class="csv2-btn csv2-btn--primary" data-role="leader">
            <i class="fas fa-star"></i>
            <span class="cs-attach-choice-label">{{localize "CS.dialogs.attachCharacter.leader"}}</span>
            <span class="cs-attach-choice-hint">{{localize "CS.dialogs.attachCharacter.leaderHint"}}</span>
        </button>
        <button type="button" class="csv2-btn csv2-btn--outline" data-role="hero">
            <i class="far fa-user"></i>
            <span class="cs-attach-choice-label">{{localize "CS.dialogs.attachCharacter.hero"}}</span>
            <span class="cs-attach-choice-hint">{{localize "CS.dialogs.attachCharacter.heroHint"}}</span>
        </button>
    </div>
</div>
